index 00000000..835a6f0c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PrimaeNative/Core/Sonification/Candidates/WorldRT/WorldRT.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,861 @@
+// WorldRT.swift
+// PrimaeNative — pitch bake-off phase 2, candidate C2 "WorldRT" (2026-11-23)
+//
+// A live source-filter vocoder (BAKEOFF-PITCH.md section 2 C2): WORLD's
+// synthesis (`synthesis.cpp`, https://github.com/mmorise/World at commit
+// c794856b537758a3d300757db2e5e31685a822c2; Morise, Yokomori & Ozawa, IEICE
+// Trans. Inf. & Syst. E99-D(7), 2016) re-cast as a pulse-at-a-time renderer
+// that runs inside a 256-frame I/O callback. NOT wired into the study path.
+//
+//   .voicedPhoneme   Init: `WorldRTAnalysis` (F0 from our marks, CheapTrick,
+//                    D4C, jitter/shimmer per mark). Render: a parameter-time
+//                    read-head advances at `rate` (time stretch by frame
+//                    interpolation, no granular repetition); the excitation
+//                    runs at F0(t) x pf, one pulse per period. On each pulse,
+//                    as WORLD's `GetOneFrameSegment`: the envelope and
+//                    aperiodicity at the read-head (frames interpolated
+//                    linearly; optionally frequency-warped by pf^gamma), a
+//                    minimum-phase response of sp x (1 - ap^2) delayed by the
+//                    pulse's sub-sample position and scaled by sqrt(interval),
+//                    plus white noise of the interval's length (a fixed,
+//                    seeded table read contiguously: one continuous noise
+//                    stream cut at the pulses, as WORLD) filtered by the
+//                    minimum-phase response of sp x ap^2; DC removed as
+//                    WORLD's `RemoveDCComponent`; overlap-added into a ring.
+//                    Minimum phase makes each response start at its pulse, so
+//                    the renderer is causal: the first half of the N = 2048
+//                    response (23 ms, tapered over its last 128 samples) is
+//                    kept, WORLD's anti-causal wrap (its fftshift) is dropped.
+//                    The recorded attack (onset .. loop start) plays exactly
+//                    as the shipped TDPSOLA plays it (same prepared copy,
+//                    rate 1, pitch unchanged), then cross-fades to the vocoder
+//                    over `handoverPeriods`; `vocodedAttack` vocodes from the
+//                    third mark instead. The loop wraps in the PARAMETER
+//                    domain: over the last `seamSeconds` before the loop end
+//                    the parameters blend (raised cosine) to those one loop
+//                    length earlier, so the wrap lands on what it blended to.
+//   .unvoicedPhoneme (F) Candidate A's branch (r28 candidate A, 5dcc4b4f), in
+//                    its continuous form: the prepared loop is read at the
+//                    pitch ratio through a Kaiser-windowed sinc (beta 8,
+//                    8 zero crossings) at min(1, 1/pf) of the source Nyquist;
+//                    rate does not move it (U1). 0 cents is sample-exact.
+//   .carrier         The shipped TDPSOLA, unchanged (composition).
+//
+// Real-time contract (as TDPSOLA): `render` and the setters allocate nothing,
+// take no lock, touch no Swift array or class reference (state behind
+// UnsafeMutablePointers allocated in init; vDSP setups created in init), and
+// read parameters from relaxed atomics holding Float bit patterns.
